Date: Sun, 12 May 2024 11:08:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 280/356] commands/ls: Fix NULL dereference

The grub_strrchr() may return NULL when the dirname do not contain "/".
This can happen on broken filesystems.

Reported-by: B Horn <b@horn.uk>
Signed-off-by: B Horn <b@horn.uk>
Reviewed-by: Daniel Kiper <daniel.kiper@oracle.com>
---
 grub-core/commands/ls.c | 11 +++++++++++
 1 file changed, 11 insertions(+)

diff --git a/grub-core/commands/ls.c b/grub-core/commands/ls.c
index c3bcb08..74d35e6 100644
--- a/grub-core/commands/ls.c
+++ b/grub-core/commands/ls.c
@@ -256,7 +256,18 @@ grub_ls_list_files (char *dirname, int longlist, int all, int human, int dirhdr)
 	    goto fail;
 	  ++(ctx.filename);
 
+<<<<<<< HEAD
 	  ctx.dirname = grub_strndup (dirname, ctx.filename - dirname);
+=======
+	  grub_file_close (file);
+
+	  p = grub_strrchr (dirname, '/');
+	  if (p == NULL)
+	    goto fail;
+	  ++p;
+
+	  ctx.dirname = grub_strndup (dirname, p - dirname);
+>>>>>>> ae2caaa (commands/ls: Fix NULL dereference)
 	  if (ctx.dirname == NULL)
 	    goto fail;
 
